cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use MiraProt in your research, please cite the MiraProt software
  release used for your analysis and the associated publication when available.

title: "MiraProt"

type: software

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-28"

authors:
  - family-names: "Schmalen"
    given-names: "Adrian"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2462-2675"

abstract: >-
  MiraProt is a modular R Shiny-based platform for integrated downstream analysis
  of processed protein-level proteomics data. It combines metadata-aware data
  preparation with differential abundance analysis, dimensionality reduction,
  functional enrichment and gene set enrichment analysis, protein interaction
  analysis, protein set comparison, and visualization within a connected
  interactive workflow. By retaining structured metadata across analysis steps,
  MiraProt facilitates consistent reuse of prepared datasets and reduces
  repeated restructuring and manual transfer of intermediate results between
  separate tools.

repository-code: "https://github.com/AdSchmalen/MiraProt"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - proteomics
  - R Shiny
  - downstream proteomics analysis
  - differential abundance
  - functional enrichment
  - data visualization
  - research software
  - metadata-aware data analysis

# Zenodo software archive

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22110860"

